NA - Debix kernel cross-compile - based on step by step instructions -> https://debix.io/Document/manual_info/id/8.html

1.
sudo apt install git bc bison flex libssl-dev make libc6-dev libncurses5-dev
sudo apt-get install qtbase5-dev qtchooser qt5-qmake qtbase5-dev-tools		# For kernel's make xconfig 
2.
sudo mkdir /opt/toolchain-debix
sudo chown nelis:nelis /opt/toolchain-debix
cd /opt/toolchain-debix
wget "https://developer.arm.com/-/media/Files/downloads/gnu-a/10.3-2021.07/binrel/gcc-arm-10.3-2021.07-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu.tar.xz?rev=1cb9c51b94f54940bdcccd791451cec3&hash=A56CA491FA630C98F7162BC1A302F869"
mv "https://developer.arm.com/-/media/Files/downloads/gnu-a/10.3-2021.07/binrel/gcc-arm-10.3-2021.07-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu.tar.xz?rev=1cb9c51b94f54940bdcccd791451cec3&hash=A56CA491FA630C98F7162BC1A302F869" gcc-arm-10.3-2021.07-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu.tar.xz
tar xpf gcc-arm-10.3-2021.07-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu.tar.xz

3.
export CROSS_COMPILE=/opt/toolchain-debix/gcc-arm-10.3-2021.07-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu/bin/aarch64-none-linux-gnu-
export ARCH=arm64

4.
cd /opt/toolchain-debix
git clone --depth=1 --branch debix https://github.com/debix-tech/linux
mv linux linux-debix

5.
cd /opt/toolchain-debix/linux-debix
make imx_v8_defconfig
make -j8
make modules

6.
make INSTALL_MOD_STRIP=1 modules_install  INSTALL_MOD_PATH=out
cd out/lib/modules/5.10.72

7. (adjust paths and drives to taste, check with 'fdisk -l')
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/fat32
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/ext4
sudo mount /dev/sde1 /mnt/fat32
sudo mount /dev/sde2 /mnt/ext4

8.
cd /opt/toolchain-debix/linux-debix
export PATH=$PATH:/opt/toolchain-debix/gcc-arm-10.3-2021.07-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu/bin
sudo env PATH=$PATH make ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-none-linux-gnu- INSTALL_MOD_PATH=/mnt/ext4 INSTALL_MOD_STRIP=1 modules_install
sudo umount /mnt/ext4

9.
sudo cp /mnt/fat32/Image /mnt/fat32/Image-backup-`date "+%s"`.img
sudo cp arch/arm64/boot/Image /mnt/fat32/Image
sudo cp arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/*.dtb /mnt/fat32
sudo umount /mnt/fat32

10. If all the steps were succesfull, you can configuring the kernel to your taste (make sure the path is still set to the one in step 8)
make ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-none-linux-gnu- menuconfig	# Text config
make ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-none-linux-gnu- xconfig		# GUI config

11. Repeat steps 5 (except make imx_v8_defconfig), 6, 7, 8 and 9 to install an updated kernel



